WEBVTT

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.220
I'll use everything I have to protect the 2nd Lieutenant.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.480
That must be...

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.620
...how this huge body should be used.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:56.920
That's because...

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.760
...I cannot allow this unfairness.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.480
"They cannot be punished because they are noble."

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.220
"They are allowed to do so because they are commoners."

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.660
That's ridiculous!

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.450
If you are guilty, then you will be punished.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:09.950
If you do evil, then I will slash you,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.610
whether you're a noble or a commoner,

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.660
or even His Majesty, the Emperor...

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.610
...that is the only justice I can display.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.100
This coat...

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:49.990
...has the smell of Section III.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.820
The territory you spoke of...

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.500
I have one now, too!

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.250
From this moment on...

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.530
...this place is the operational area...

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.910
...of the war relief unit, Pumpkin Scissors!

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.050
Oh!

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.180
I found some potatoes!

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:29.330
We must~ eat it~ all up~ okay~?

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.190
I wonder if he'll be happy when I bring this back.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.440
Mer-kun~

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.190
M-Mer-kun?!

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.790
That's embezzling rations, you know?

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.520
C-C-Captain?!

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:48.520
Ah, b-but, these are all burnt up anyway.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.670
U-Um... I-I... U-Um...

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.330
Where are the other three?

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.370
You guys should've been back hours ago.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.150
You guys are always like this, for crying out loud.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:02.120
Yeah...

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.570
So... umm...

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.180
Come straight home sometimes.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.260
No!

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.680
This place isn't the marshes of Loderia!

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.000
Guys...

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.190
The hesitation in her steps is gone.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.970
Perhaps, it's because of who you are.

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:04.190
Your sword strikes are really straightforward,

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.640
and thus easy to read.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.910
This... is a noble?

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.790
Damn, she was close!

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.120
N-No, I'm not...

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.800
...taking the side of that noblewoman...

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.870
Whatever speech she gave,

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:09.470
nothing would matter if she doesn't win.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.910
I want to just smash this duel out of the way right now.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:13.600
H-Hey!

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:27.220
Hey!

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.680
Someone give me some help here!

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.200
We can do this if we all attack him at the same time!

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:33.250
B-But...

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.740
Don't worry!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.540
This guy's all injured!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.560
And killing this injured guy...

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.330
...are we still acting justly?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.930
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.250
Who cares about justice, anymore?!

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.040
But then-

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.200
Have you forgotten what they've done?

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.240
I know!

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.820
But, that doesn't mean-

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:58.770
Maybe this way was wrong after all.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.770
Why you...

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.040
What about you guys?!

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.120
But...

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.820
That's why they should've just stayed as a mob.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:13.240
They're not all composed of people who could care less about using justice as an excuse.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.080
If they wanted to kill you,

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.190
then they shouldn't have talked about justice.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:27.820
Why do I have to be hated so much?

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.410
Assuming...

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.690
I mean assuming...

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:35.710
...assuming I embezzled money...

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:39.590
It's not as if I had killed someone!

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:42.690
I did eat delicious food!

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:46.110
But is that something to be so jealous about that they want to kill me?!

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.630
Is it?

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:53.900
From what I just heard...

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.600
That guy that appears to be their leader...

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.660
He's been through a lot of things, hasn't he?

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.030
So what?

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:05.490
Is he trying to say that if I hadn't embezzled, his children would have survived?

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.960
How ridiculous!

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.580
Of course not.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.200
He knows that things aren't that naive in this world.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:17.280
Besides, even if the money you embezzled was used properly,

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:23.890
what the civilians see is just whether or not there's an extra grain of rice in their hands.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:26.900
But, you see...

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.180
If they were able to put that extra grain of rice inside their mouths...

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:35.390
...if they were able to live a bit longer from that grain of rice...

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:40.330
...they could have heard one more word from their children.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.560
Perhaps they could have stood up in life had they heard that word.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:51.030
What you took away from them are those grains of rice.

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:52.900
Try calculating it...

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.210
...how much wheat could have been bought...

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:57.840
...with the money you spent having fun?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.850
That's basically it.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.260
I was right.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.820
Although slowly,

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.160
the road lights on the way towards this ballroom are getting turned off.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.620
This place has been smelled out by Section I.

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:29.130
Even if the LT wins the duel,

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:33.880
would Section I accept the terms that Leonir Taylor proposed?

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.130
But...

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:40.140
...I don't think they'd put down their weapons easily...

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:44.140
We need something...
to make them lay down their weapons...

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:48.100
We can't let you go through here,

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:52.290
even if it's you, Section III chief, Captain Hunks.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.030
Ah, I see.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:58.060
Besides, you're not even on duty right now.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:00.050
Please don't interfere with Section I's...

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.910
...with the army's operations.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:05.830
Hmm...

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.130
I thought I saw something crawl up...

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.130
Given that height...

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:19.720
...it must have been a cat...

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.160
Captain! Welcome back!

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.000
How did it go?

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.780
Section I's siege has been set.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.780
No one will be able to escape.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.430
All of them will be captured,

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.650
and their entire families will be tortured.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.030
Our entire families...

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:46.480
Our family...

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:49.330
Our families have nothing to do with this.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:51.940
Don't worry!

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.750
Alice and the others are there.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:59.130
And Mer-kun must be bringing them some kind of secret plan, right, Captain?

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.640
There's such a thing?

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.080
Then what did you give him?

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.670
It almost escaped me,

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:21.360
but for Section III, Alice L. Malvin,
may not always be the correct answer.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.680
Looks like the first half of the duel has taken its toll on you.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.350
You used too much unnecessary energy, didn't you?

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:00.780
2nd Lieutenant!

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.030
A noble's...

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:38.770
All nobles'...

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:43.610
...pride.

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.680
This duel is over.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.350
This duel is not yet over.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:11.360
2nd Lieutenant...

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:15.840
But... if she's scrambling for her breath so much...

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.530
...she won't be able to take the Royal Guard's attack...

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:22.540
I must not let that happen...

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.960
I may still be in training,

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.950
but if it's one-on-one...

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:32.740
...I can finish this!

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:35.950
My princess should be right-handed.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.630
Are you planning on taking on my sword with your left hand?

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:42.130
How amusing.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:43.840
Then take this!

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:55.760
She bounced it back?!

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:57.850
No, that's not it.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.720
Without a doubt, she used my power to deflect it back.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:15.250
But with the same power as before,
she derailed the trajectory of my strike?!

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:20.540
She brought her sword together with mine and just changed its trajectory?

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:26.400
And... this unique and clear sound...

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:29.740
It can't be!

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.380
A long time ago,

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:35.820
when my grandfather helped bring down the civil war in your country,

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:39.300
he received three gifts from the former King.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:46.190
One was the nickname of the Noble Flamme.

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:51.860
One was the great sword, Noble Flamme.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.080
And the last one...

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.980
...when he was assaulted by young soldiers on the streets...

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:00.840
...he had no choice but to cut them down and lamented...

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.460
...so the King personally taught him
His own defensive sword techniques...

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:23.200
...the unreachable Main Gauche...

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:26.920
So that's how it is... but...

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:30.920
...against a foreigner's crude imitation of Loderia's sword technique,

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.740
we Royal Guards cannot lose.

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:38.540
Our King's... our Royalty's sword!!

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:50.630
It is strange...

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:54.390
I have not had much success with this all these years,

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.560
and my body is all worn out,

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:03.310
but when I realize that I am before these guys,

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.430
I can move so freely...

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.420
So freely!

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.930
That girl...

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.440
For being so bad at dancing...

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:39.880
I've forgotten...

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:41.940
...to breathe...

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:59.710
I've held the sheath with my right hand and tried drawing the sword with my left hand for years.

00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:01.970
Now that I'm finally able to use it correctly,

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.330
I've come to realize something.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:07.540
Guarding doesn't fit my style.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:11.050
My princess has caught her breath.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:14.390
"Finally able to use it"... how conceited of you...

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.590
Here I go!

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:18.640
She's fast!

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:21.890
Although the power of her strike is weaker compared to her right hand,

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:24.150
her left hand is fast!

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:28.960
I screwed up.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:32.390
I lost my calm over Loderia's prestige.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.740
Or... is there something that is lighting the fire under this noble?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.000
No...

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:46.080
I was...

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:49.570
...just too immature...

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:08.510
I took the liberty to pull a little prank for what you did to my dress.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:13.790
I am not as straightforward as you say I am.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:21.280
Victory is yours...

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:24.550
...Noble Flamme.

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:35.460
That's got to hurt.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:44.610
I say, young man.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:47.980
If she's a "noble",

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.590
what do people see me as?

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:56.730
Just a noble that committed a crime.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:18:59.650
A-A noble...

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:03.130
2nd Lieutenant.

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:04.820
I am all right.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:06.240
Do not worry.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.920
Malvin won, that means-

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:11.750
We're safe... right?

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:15.040
If we put down our weapons now, we'll be innocent.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.690
Can we go home?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.240
Don't let them confuse you!

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.970
We didn't come here to watch that duel.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.230
We came here to kill nobles, right?!

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:36.020
But that was because we thought
we were carrying out an act of justice.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:37.860
Are you just scared of capital punishment?!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:40.110
That's not it...

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.640
It's that woman...

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.870
It's because of that woman that everyone's gone weird.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.030
If it weren't for you!!!

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:49.460
Corporal!

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.170
A-A military hound?!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.390
Mercury!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.340
It's from the Captain!

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:11.230
What?!

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.350
Fourth Axe mobilized the cops?!

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.100
We're completely surrounded.

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:30.370
So even if we did persuade
these guys to put their weapons down,

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:35.240
we're no longer able to return them home secretly, eh?

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:39.170
And we don't have any time left either.

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:42.170
The encirclement is collapsing.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:49.310
Maybe it's an assault that doesn't involve any rescuing.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:52.440
And what about this one?

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:54.890
A simple authorization document.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.980
Then it's really no different than
the usual Section III authorizations.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.560
The LT's here.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:05.400
Even without these documents, authorizations like these-

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:07.470
These aren't for the 2nd Lieutenant!

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:10.210
These are all for Sergeant Major use.

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:11.850
For us?

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:12.960
Ah-

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.050
Wait,

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:15.920
we still need to...

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:19.460
...have them drop their weapons first.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:24.440
You guys came here to exert your anger on nobles.

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:26.850
There's no way you'd accept an end like this.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:29.870
Come.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:31.130
I'll take on all of it.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.640
2nd Lieutenant!

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:33.060
Mer-kun, it's time for the final episode.

00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:36.060
To protect, to be protected, our battle shall continue...

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:38.330
...because we want to see the smile on everyone's face!

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.300
Next time, "Soldiers - Commoners - Nobles"

00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:43.640
Let's go! It's time for war relief!
